    "notes": "Segment start is the 0-based offset in the electronic-format IBAN (no spaces); values.characterClass uses the SWIFT classes n (digits), a (upper-case letters), c (upper-case letters and digits). This format is not registered with SWIFT. Treat it as a hint for display and soft validation, not as a rule. Disagreements in other libraries, recorded but not followed: bankCode position in the BBAN: php-iban has 0-3, schwifty has 0-5; branchCode position in the BBAN: php-iban has 3-8, schwifty has 5-10; nationalCheckDigits position in the BBAN: php-iban has 22-25, schwifty has 22-24."
